  "solution": {
    "text": "In the neutralization of acid and base <math><mi>N</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>V</mi></math> of both must be equivalent<br /><br /><math><mi>N</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>V</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>0.1</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>100</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>10</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mi>N</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>V</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>O</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>0.2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>ml</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mi>NaOH</mi></munder><mfenced><mi>ml</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mfenced><mi>ml</mi></mfenced></mrow><mi>KOH</mi></munder></math><br /><br /><math><mn>0.1</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>100</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>0.2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.25</mn><mo>×</mo><mi>V</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mn>10</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.25</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>V</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>400</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>25</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>16</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></math>",
